{
    "0": {
        "0_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<ts$Ariya  $Marisa  $Enoko  >Deep below the Asama Purifying Mountain."
            ]
        },
        "1_0": {
            "lines": [
                "After a grueling battle, Marisa Kirisame",
                "defeated Ariya Iwanaga, the goddess of unchanging."
            ]
        },
        "6_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<l$> However...”"
            ]
        },
        "7_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Ariya  >“A torrent of impurity from the Outside World will also rush in."
            ]
        },
        "8_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<l$> What happens after that... is in your hands.”"
            ]
        },
        "10_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Ariya  >“Why don’t you witness for yourself how Gensokyo changes?”"
            ]
        },
        "11_0": {
            "lines": [
                "The Forest of Magic."
            ]
        },
        "40_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<c$Congratulations!$>",
                "<c$Congratulations on your No Continue Clear!$>"
            ]
        },
        "2_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Ariya  >“That Incident Stone was certainly the real deal."
            ]
        },
        "3_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<l$> Thanks to you, I can take some time off work. I'm grateful.”"
            ]
        },
        "4_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Marisa  >“Wait, return Gensokyo to normal first!”"
            ]
        },
        "5_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Ariya  >“You needn’t worry. Once I withdraw my power, Gensokyo should return to normal."
            ]
        },
        "9_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Marisa  >“What? ‘In my hands’...? What do you mean?”"
            ]
        },
        "12_0": {
            "lines": [
                "A deep, dark forest where all manner of evil spirits creep ever closer."
            ]
        },
        "13_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Enoko  >“Heey, Marisa! What’s with that stone?”"
            ]
        },
        "14_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Marisa  >“This here? It’s called an Incident Stone. For some weird reason,",
                "<l$> it’s loaded with an incident’s power.”"
            ]
        },
        "15_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Enoko  >“Incident’s power? What’s that?”"
            ]
        },
        "16_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Marisa  >“An incident is an incident, it’s when things aren’t normal.”"
            ]
        },
        "17_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Enoko  >“That’s not much of an explanation.",
                "<l$> But hey, this Incident Stone... it feels like that person.”"
            ]
        },
        "18_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Marisa  >“Spot on, that’s one sharp nose."
            ]
        },
        "19_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<l$> It’s the magic aura of that oni from Hell, Zanmu.”"
            ]
        },
        "20_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Enoko  >“Should you really be carrying around something so eerie?”"
            ]
        },
        "21_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Marisa  >“Strangely enough, thanks to this Incident Stone,",
                "<l$> I was able to resolve the incident this time around.”"
            ]
        },
        "22_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Enoko  >“So you were dancing in the palm of her hand again, were you?”"
            ]
        },
        "23_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Marisa  >“No clue, it was one odd incident though.”"
            ]
        },
        "24_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Marisa  >“You didn’t even notice it either, right? The incident in Gensokyo.”"
            ]
        },
        "25_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Enoko  >“Well, you see, I haven’t left the forest."
            ]
        },
        "26_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<l$> But it did feel oddly boring.”"
            ]
        },
        "27_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Marisa  >“That’s it, the boredom. That’s what this incident was.”"
            ]
        },
        "28_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Enoko  >“The boredom was the incident? You sure it’s not all in your head?”"
            ]
        },
        "29_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<r$Marisa  >“Don’t be stupid, has Gensokyo ever been boring?"
            ]
        },
        "30_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<l$> Sure, for an hour or two it happens, but I’d die of boredom if it lasted for days."
            ]
        },
        "31_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<l$> That deadly kind of boredom is what happened.”"
            ]
        },
        "32_0": {
            "lines": [
                "When Enoko, who had been feeling bored, came over to talk, Marisa’s interest piqued."
            ]
        },
        "33_0": {
            "lines": [
                "She felt that Gensokyo is starting to move again."
            ]
        },
        "34_0": {
            "lines": [
                "She couldn’t yet sense any major changes of the sort Ariya had spoken of..."
            ]
        },
        "35_0": {
            "lines": [
                "Or rather, did returning to how things were before itself count as a change?"
            ]
        },
        "36_0": {
            "lines": [
                "Even if an immense amount of impurity flowed in from the Outside World,",
                "Gensokyo would probably be fine."
            ]
        },
        "37_0": {
            "lines": [
                "That’s because it’s Gensokyo’s nature to simply accept such things."
            ]
        },
        "38_0": {
            "lines": [
                "However, if it ever starts to reject change,",
                "perhaps that will be the moment when Gensokyo will truly die."
            ]
        },
        "39_0": {
            "lines": [
                "<c$Ending No.15 — Boredom is a Creeping Death$>"
            ]
        }
    }
}